# The W1/W6 vault-I/O fixture corpus deliberately contains specific
# byte-for-byte content (CRLF, mixed line endings, a UTF-8 BOM, no
# trailing newline) that the round-trip tests assert is preserved
# exactly. Without this, Git's line-ending normalization (core.autocrlf)
# would silently rewrite CRLF -> LF on commit/checkout and quietly
# invalidate the fixtures. Mark them binary so Git never touches them.
packages/citrinium_core/test/fixtures/** -text
